  "term": "dedifferentiation",
  "definition": "Dedifferentiation is the process by which a more specialized cell shifts back toward a less specialized, more plastic, progenitor-like state. In the source context, this change is linked to regained capacity for proliferation, migration, and later neuronal differentiation.",
